<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Robot Combat Tournament Rules</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary: #ff4500;
            --dark: #1a1a1a;
            --light: #f4f4f4;
            --gray: #2d2d2d;
            --text-light: #ffffff;
            --text-dark: #333333;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: var(--light);
            color: var(--text-dark);
        }

        header {
            background-color: var(--dark);
            color: var(--text-light);
            padding: 2rem 1rem;
            text-align: center;
            border-bottom: 5px solid var(--primary);
        }

        header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
        }

        header p {
            margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
            color: #bbb;
        }

        main {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 2rem auto;
            padding: 0 1rem;
        }

        .rule-section {
            background: #fff;
            padding: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            border-left: 5px solid var(--primary);
            border-radius: 4px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        .rule-section h2 {
            margin-top: 0;
            color: var(--dark);
            text-transform: uppercase;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.5rem;
        }

        .rule-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding: 0;
            margin: 0;
        }

        .rule-list li {
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            padding-left: 1.5rem;
            position: relative;
        }

        .rule-list li::before {
            content: "•";
            color: var(--primary);
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            top: -2px;
        }

        .rule-list li strong {
            color: var(--dark);
        }

        .warning-box {
            background-color: #fff3cd;
            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;
            color: #856404;
            padding: 1rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            margin-top: 1rem;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 2rem;
            background-color: var(--dark);
            color: var(--text-light);
            margin-top: 3rem;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Robot Combat Official Rules</h1>
        <p>Standard Regulations & Safety Guidelines</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <!-- Weight Classes -->
        <section class="rule-section">
            <h2>⚙️ 1. Weight Classes & Inspection</h2>
            <ul class="rule-list">
                <li><strong>Strict Limits:</strong> All robots must strictly fit within their registered weight class limits (e.g., 150g Fairyweight, 1lb Antweight, 3lb Beetleweight).</li>
                <li><strong>Safety Inspection:</strong> Every robot must pass a mandatory safety tech check before entering the arena.</li>
                <li><strong>Activation Switch:</strong> Robots must feature an explicit, easily accessible power switch or removable link to deactivate the system safely.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Match Rules -->
        <section class="rule-section">
            <h2>⚔️ 2. Match & Combat Rules</h2>
            <ul class="rule-list">
                <li><strong>Match Duration:</strong> Standard matches last 3 minutes unless a knockout occurs.</li>
                <li><strong>Tap-Outs:</strong> A builder may forfeit the match at any time by calling a verbal "Tap-Out".</li>
                <li><strong>Mobility:</strong> Robots must demonstrate controlled translational movement. If a robot cannot move due to damage, a 10-second countdown will begin.</li>
                <li><strong>Pinning & Lifting:</strong> Robots may pin or lift an opponent for a maximum of 10 seconds before they must release them.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Prohibited Weapons -->
        <section class="rule-section">
            <h2>🚫 3. Prohibited Weapons & Tactics</h2>
            <ul class="rule-list">
                <li><strong>Radio Interference:</strong> Any intentional jamming or interference with opponent control frequencies is strictly banned.</li>
                <li><strong>Liquid & Gas:</strong> Liquid weapons, smoke generation, and unapproved pressurized gas systems are forbidden.</li>
                <li><strong>Arena Damage:</strong> Weapons explicitly designed to deliberately destroy or chew into the arena floor or walls are prohibited.</li>
                <li><strong>Untethered Projectiles:</strong> Projectiles must be securely tethered to the robot body unless explicitly permitted by specific event variants.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="warning-box">
                <strong>⚠️ Safety Violations:</strong> Failure to comply with weapon safety restrictions will result in immediate disqualification from the tournament.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Judging Criteria -->
        <section class="rule-section">
            <h2>⚖️ 4. Judging Criteria</h2>
            <p>If a match goes to the full time limit, three judges will score the fight based on:</p>
            <ul class="rule-list">
                <li><strong>Damage:</strong> Points awarded for visible structural or functional harm inflicted on the opponent.</li>
                <li><strong>Aggression:</strong> Points awarded for frequency and severity of intentional attacks.</li>
                <li><strong>Control:</strong> Points awarded for dictating the pace and orientation of the fight.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Robot Combat Association. All Rights Reserved.</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
